1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,850
I want you to crawl over with love.

2
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:05,230
With love. And then?

3
00:00:05,670 --> 00:00:09,010
Crawl over and show your love.

4
00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:11,230
Do you know how to show love?

5
00:00:13,830 --> 00:00:16,870
It's that simple.

6
00:00:18,567 --> 00:00:20,667
You just need to crawl over.

7
00:00:22,627 --> 00:00:23,587
That's all.

8
00:00:23,587 --> 00:00:25,567
No. No.

9
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:27,187
Tell me why I have to crawl.

10
00:00:37,527 --> 00:00:40,887
Have you thought about what this character means?

11
00:00:41,487 --> 00:00:43,007
Tell me. I'm listening.

12
00:00:43,007 --> 00:00:46,067
You have to convince me, director.

13
00:00:47,747 --> 00:00:49,407
If you don't need to crawl

14
00:00:49,967 --> 00:00:52,867
to show your state after death,

15
00:00:54,127 --> 00:00:55,287
you can fly instead.

16
00:00:56,127 --> 00:00:57,167
When did I die?

17
00:00:59,747 --> 00:01:01,367
Fine. You didn't die.

18
00:01:07,147 --> 00:01:09,127
How could you not be dead?

19
00:01:12,527 --> 00:01:13,427
Don't rush.

20
00:01:14,027 --> 00:01:17,147
You're getting confused. Think about the script.

21
00:01:17,827 --> 00:01:20,807
There is no dialogue here, but it clearly says:

22
00:01:23,167 --> 00:01:28,807
Strangled by those steel-like wrists,

23
00:01:28,807 --> 00:01:30,887
he slowly stops breathing,

24
00:01:31,787 --> 00:01:33,487
then drifts away like a ghost.

25
00:01:34,375 --> 00:01:36,175
He drifts away like a ghost.

26
00:01:36,175 --> 00:01:37,955
Didn't you read it?

27
00:01:39,515 --> 00:01:41,055
Crawled over like a ghost?

28
00:01:41,935 --> 00:01:46,075
Then float. If you can float, good for you.

29
00:01:49,075 --> 00:01:53,475
I can't float. Why did you write it?

30
00:01:58,735 --> 00:02:00,715
Didn't you read the script and agree to act in it?

31
00:02:02,055 --> 00:02:04,815
Didn't you say the script was written just for me?

32
00:02:06,075 --> 00:02:07,115
Show me how to float.

33
00:02:10,995 --> 00:02:12,415
Let's do this...

34
00:02:14,435 --> 00:02:14,875
Wait.

35
00:02:14,875 --> 00:02:21,155
We said it was written for you, and you agreed. Right?

36
00:02:22,883 --> 00:02:26,083
I'd like to crawl, but that isn't me. It's you.

37
00:02:26,083 --> 00:02:28,783
I want to, but that character isn't me. It's you.

38
00:02:28,883 --> 00:02:32,423
You crawl. Why does it have to be me, not you?

39
00:02:33,783 --> 00:02:38,083
Crawl first. Then we'll talk.

40
00:02:38,083 --> 00:02:39,963
You went to see the moon, not me.

41
00:02:41,903 --> 00:02:45,003
You went to see the moon. I didn't.

42
00:02:45,003 --> 00:02:46,423
All right.

43
00:02:47,583 --> 00:02:48,503
I understand you.

44
00:02:51,363 --> 00:02:53,463
You understand me?

45
00:02:53,883 --> 00:02:56,743
I know you're willing to let him go. Right?

46
00:02:56,743 --> 00:03:00,003
You are given death, but won't become a ghost...

47
00:03:01,403 --> 00:03:02,443
and express your love.

48
00:03:04,803 --> 00:03:11,763
Doesn't it say he drifts away like a ghost?

49
00:03:11,763 --> 00:03:16,163
I'm the director.

50
00:03:19,083 --> 00:03:22,943
If that feeling comes across, you're a good actor.

51
00:03:22,943 --> 00:03:25,643
But you resist it. Can't you try?

52
00:03:27,452 --> 00:03:28,852
You really don't love him.

53
00:03:31,072 --> 00:03:32,252
What gives you the right to say that?

54
00:03:38,592 --> 00:03:40,612
You won't even get down on all fours.

55
00:03:44,112 --> 00:03:44,992
Are you too noble for that?

56
00:03:48,192 --> 00:03:56,572
We were animals. Does becoming human change that?

57
00:03:58,172 --> 00:04:00,132
Even dead, you are an animal. You can still crawl.

58
00:04:02,883 --> 00:04:04,283
I was impulsive just now.

59
00:04:11,663 --> 00:04:16,923
Let me explain why I designed it this way.

60
00:04:18,523 --> 00:04:20,823
Look at the words. What do they say?

61
00:04:21,083 --> 00:04:22,703
Why are you me?

62
00:04:24,023 --> 00:04:25,123
Why am I me?

63
00:04:25,283 --> 00:04:26,483
Why am I not me?

64
00:04:28,123 --> 00:04:28,743
Right?

65
00:04:29,403 --> 00:04:33,043
You're still you, but you're no longer yourself.

66
00:04:33,043 --> 00:04:36,563
What does that mean? You are changing.

67
00:04:37,083 --> 00:04:40,443
Your memories may remain, but your body has changed.

68
00:04:41,203 --> 00:04:45,543
Doesn't that mean you've become a ghost?

69
00:04:46,043 --> 00:04:46,843
A ghost.

70
00:04:48,075 --> 00:04:51,095
It's my fault. My fault.

71
00:04:52,115 --> 00:04:52,875
It isn't your fault?

72
00:04:52,875 --> 00:04:56,255
You won't do this little scene. You just keep arguing.

73
00:04:57,727 --> 00:05:05,147
Do you understand what play you want to make? I doubt it.

74
00:05:07,427 --> 00:05:11,887
You don't understand, so you can't give that love.

75
00:05:14,427 --> 00:05:17,767
Play? Is making theatre just a game to you?

76
00:05:18,987 --> 00:05:23,427
You told me: my soul has been transformed.

77
00:05:23,427 --> 00:05:25,967
You said you saw something in this play. Was it all false?

78
00:05:25,967 --> 00:05:30,447
You saw your former self and wanted to find it again.

79
00:05:32,907 --> 00:05:35,667
This isn't me giving you a chance. We're collaborating.

80
00:05:36,467 --> 00:05:39,367
I'm lucky to have both of you.

81
00:05:40,287 --> 00:05:45,247
Just this scene. Then we can wrap for today.

82
00:05:48,987 --> 00:05:50,247
So how will your soul be transformed?

83
00:05:52,027 --> 00:05:55,287
You do it. Then I'll do it.

84
00:05:59,247 --> 00:06:00,467
I can't become you.

85
00:06:00,467 --> 00:06:01,887
You don't have to become me.

86
00:06:03,167 --> 00:06:06,587
You didn't write this play for me. You wrote it for yourself.

87
00:06:06,587 --> 00:06:09,907
What do you take me for?

88
00:06:12,727 --> 00:06:14,187
Don't you think that's childish?

89
00:06:16,087 --> 00:06:16,767
I won't say it.

90
00:06:22,847 --> 00:06:23,687
Hearing you say that...

91
00:06:27,367 --> 00:06:29,007
I thought you were happy with the script.

92
00:06:30,187 --> 00:06:33,827
There are only two days left.

93
00:06:45,627 --> 00:06:52,207
Will it work? Will anyone come to see it?

94
00:06:55,327 --> 00:06:59,147
If people come, I'll split the ticket money with you.

95
00:06:59,827 --> 00:07:01,147
It isn't about money.

96
00:07:02,955 --> 00:07:04,255
It's about your attitude.

97
00:07:06,275 --> 00:07:07,315
I think I'm taking this seriously.

98
00:07:08,095 --> 00:07:09,495
We took it seriously when we came.

99
00:07:10,995 --> 00:07:12,895
Now it's all been worn away.

100
00:07:13,995 --> 00:07:17,855
You don't understand love. How can I be patient?

101
00:07:18,755 --> 00:07:21,055
This is all I can do. Why did you choose me?

102
00:07:22,715 --> 00:07:24,575
I can't give you any more. All right?

103
00:07:24,575 --> 00:07:26,335
You had the right feeling. That's why I chose you.

104
00:07:32,455 --> 00:07:35,755
My head is a mess...

105
00:07:43,775 --> 00:07:45,675
Then it's over. It's that simple.

106
00:07:45,675 --> 00:07:48,675
All right. Don't crawl. Walk over.

107
00:08:14,475 --> 00:08:16,975
All right. Is that enough?

108
00:08:18,495 --> 00:08:23,675
All right.

109
00:08:28,775 --> 00:08:31,735
I've had enough. I've had enough.

110
00:08:33,755 --> 00:08:34,575
Is that enough?

111
00:08:34,575 --> 00:08:36,835
All right. We're done. Let's eat.
